    card title "What's your name?"

A: How do you ask someone's name in Russian, and how do you give yours?
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name

B: Tom and I first met a year ago, in a café. Listen to how we got talking.
    highlight tom masha color #c9871a effect pulse

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

A: Как тебя́ зову́т? means what's your name, but word for word it asks: how do they call you?
    highlight talk_1_words color #c9871a part "Как тебя́ зову́т"

A: That's lesson seventeen's как, how: in Russian you ask how someone is called, never что, what.
    highlight talk_1_words color #c9871a part ^Как

B: Зову́т means they call. So my answer, меня́ зову́т Ма́ша, says: me, they call Masha.
    highlight talk_2_words color #c9871a part "Меня́ зову́т"

A: Зову́т is in three of the four lines, and it never changes.
    highlight talk_1_words talk_2_words talk_3_words color #c9871a part зову́т

B: Only the word in front of it changes: тебя́, you, in Tom's question,
    highlight talk_1_words color #c9871a part тебя́

B: and меня́, me, in our answers.
    highlight talk_2_words talk_3_words color #c9871a part Меня́

B: And а тебя́? means and you? It saves asking the whole question again.
    highlight talk_2_words color #c9871a part тебя́

B: Then I said о́чень прия́тно: very pleasant, or nice to meet you. О́чень is lesson nineteen's very.
    highlight talk_4_words color #c9871a

    erase talk

    hide masha masha_name

B: Last week Tom came to my home and met my brother.
    draw masha2 masha2_name bro

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

    draw bro_name

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

A: Его́ зову́т Ива́н: him, they call Ivan. His name is Ivan.
    highlight talk2_2_words color #c9871a

    draw note_ego

B: Listen to его́: it's written with г, but said ye-VO, like the г in сего́дня.
    highlight talk2_2_words color #c9871a part Его́

    erase note_ego talk2

    draw line_eyo

A: And for a she, like Masha, it's её: её зову́т Ма́ша.
    highlight masha2 color #c9871a effect pulse

    erase line_eyo bro bro_name masha2 masha2_name

    hide speakers

A: So here's the whole set. Я becomes меня́: меня́ зову́т Том.
    draw p0 f0 x0

B: Меня́ is me as the one they call, like ма́му in lesson fourteen, the mum you see.
    highlight f0 color #c9871a

B: Ты becomes тебя́: как тебя́ зову́т?
    draw p1 f1 x1

A: Он becomes его́: его́ зову́т Ива́н.
    draw p2 f2 x2

B: Она́ becomes её: её зову́т Ма́ша.
    draw p3 f3 x3

A: And вы becomes вас: как вас зову́т?
    draw p4 f4 x4

B: That's the one for someone you'd greet with здра́вствуйте, as in lesson three, or for more than one person.
    highlight x4 color #c9871a part вас

B: Whoever it is, зову́т stays put, and so does the name; you only pick the word in front.
    highlight f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 color #c9871a

    hide board

    quiz "You meet Masha's teacher for the first time. What do you ask?" store q1 reveal.text "Здра́вствуйте! Как вас зову́т?" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 340 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: A teacher you've just met gets вы, so вас.
        wrong: Would you greet her with приве́т, or with здра́вствуйте?
        * Как тебя́ зову́т?
        + Как вас зову́т?

    icon q_teacher size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["teacher","woman"] icon_look picture of "woman teacher"

    pause 2

    erase q_teacher q1_stamp

    ask "You're Tom. Tell Masha your name: … зову́т Том. Type the missing word." answer ["меня"] store a2 default меня reveal.text "Меня́ зову́т Том." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 340 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЫЬЭЮЯ
        right: Меня́: me, they call Tom.
        wrong: Not я: the word for me, as in Masha's own answer.

    icon q_tom size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["person"] icon_look picture of man

    pause 2

    erase q_tom a2_stamp

    quiz "Tom tells a friend about Masha's brother: … зову́т Ива́н. Pick the missing word." store q3 reveal.text "Его́ зову́т Ива́н." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 340 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Ivan is a he, and it's said ye-VO.
        wrong: Ivan is a he: which word goes with он?
        * Меня́
        + Его́
        * Её

    icon q_bro size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["bearded person","man"] icon_look picture of "man: beard"

    pause 2

    erase q_bro q3_stamp

    quiz "Which question asks Masha her name?" store q4 reveal.text "Как тебя́ зову́т?" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 340 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: Russians ask how you are called, not what.
        wrong: Word for word it's how do they call you?
        * Что тебя́ зову́т?
        + Как тебя́ зову́т?

    icon q_masha size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["girl"] icon_look picture of woman

    pause 2

    erase q_masha q4_stamp

    quiz "Tom says Меня́ зову́т Том. What does Masha say next?" store q5 reveal.text "О́чень прия́тно!" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 340 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Very pleasant, which is nice to meet you.
        wrong: They have only just met. Which did Masha say in the café?
        + О́чень прия́тно!
        * Пожа́луйста!
        * До свида́ния!

    icon q_hand size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["waving hand"] icon_look picture of handshake

    pause 2

    erase q_hand q5_stamp

    show board

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

B: So Russians don't say my name is; they say they call me: меня́ зову́т.
    highlight p0 f0 x0 color #c9871a

A: The word in front changes with the person, and when you meet, it's о́чень прия́тно.
    highlight f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 color #c9871a

    hide board

    show speakers

B: Your turn, then. Как тебя́ зову́т? Say it out loud: меня́ зову́т, and your name.
    text end_q "Как тебя́ зову́т?" #3d3833 say "Как тебя зовут?" say_voice b x 500 y 600 font_size 72
    text end_a "Меня́ зову́т …" #3d3833 colors {"^Меня́":"#2f6b8f"} x 500 y 470 font_size 72

A: О́чень прия́тно! Пока́!
    text end_op "О́чень прия́тно!" #3d3833 say "Очень приятно!" say_voice a x 500 y 230 font_size 64

